.TH "SPGEN-PROJECTOR" "1" "" "spgen 0.1.0" ""
.SH NAME
spgen\-projector \- Generates a projector clause for an event and registers the projector
.SH SYNOPSIS
mix sp.gen.projector [options] <EVENT>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Applies a fact to the read model(s). One clause per projected event.
.SH Prerequisite
.IP \[bu] 2
The Domain Model (../../../../domain\-model/README.md) has a projection on the read model naming this event.
.SH "What the generator does"
use Commanded.Projections.Ecto with application, repo, the projection name (<composite>.<domain_object>_projection), schema_prefix and consistency: :strong; the project/3 clause; the child in the nearest supervisor (composite first, else subdomain — created when missing); and the event test's describe "Projector".
.PP
The clause body is derived, not chosen: SpGen.Context reads the read model's projection rule (Esdm.projection_effect/1) and emits insert, update\-from\-get_changes/1, or delete — a missing row is a no\-op for update and delete. \-\-template is validated at the CLI; the body follows the model.
.SH "Left to you"
.IP \[bu] 2
Check the clause against the rule. A projection rule whose prose states no effect falls back to create; if the model says otherwise, say so in the rule.
.IP \[bu] 2
Anything that is not row CRUD — a computed column, a second read model, a side effect — is spec logic, added inside the generated clause.
.SH Tests
In the event test (./event\-test.md), under describe "Projector": the generated case calls handle/2 with a full metadata map — handler_name equals the projector's name: option, event_number is a unique non\-negative integer — and asserts the row after an update or delete projection by first projecting the citizen's create event. Its idempotency and error cases are still manual (Known gaps (../../README.md#known\-gaps)).
.SS "Generated files"
.IP \[bu] 2
services/api/lib/sportipedia/<_subdomain>/<composite>/<domain_object>/projector.ex (projection clause per event)
.IP \[bu] 2
services/api/lib/sportipedia/<_subdomain>/<composite>/supervisor.ex (composite projector children)
.IP \[bu] 2
services/api/lib/sportipedia/<_subdomain>/supervisor.ex (fallback projector children)
.IP \[bu] 2
services/api/test/sportipedia/<_subdomain>/<composite>/<domain_object>/events/<_event>_test.exs (projected row test per fact)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-subdomain\fR \fI<SUBDOMAIN>\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-composite\fR \fI<COMPOSITE>\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-constituent\fR \fI<CONSTITUENT>\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-model\fR \fI<MODEL>\fR
model root, default docs/domain\-model (relative to \-\-root)
.TP
\fB\-\-root\fR \fI<ROOT>\fR
repo root, default inferred from the current directory
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
report the drift, write nothing
.TP
\fB\-\-template\fR \fI<TEMPLATE>\fR
what the operation does: create|update|delete|none (optional: the model declares the operation for this element)
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
create
.IP \(bu 2
update
.IP \(bu 2
delete
.IP \(bu 2
none
.RE
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-force\fR
FE: rewrite present generated units in place
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIEVENT\fR>
the element: esdm: reference, *.esdm.yaml, kind.name, or bare name
.SH "SEE ALSO"
